<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#advocate-of-the-holy-sepulchre">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Advocate of the Holy Sepulchre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1099</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Advocatus Sancti Sepulchri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Advocate of the Holy Sepulchre was the title taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-of-bouillon">Godfrey of Bouillon</a> after the crusaders captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1099, when he declined to be called king. According to tradition he refused to wear a crown of gold where Christ had worn a crown of thorns. He governed the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> until his death in 1100, after which his brother Baldwin I was crowned king.</p></div>
